<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Syphax</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 202 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Syphax was king of the Masaesyli of western Numidia in the late 3rd century BCE, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siga">Siga</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cirta">Cirta</a>. Courted by both <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a>, he sided with Carthage after marrying <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sophonisba">Sophonisba</a>. Roman and Massylian forces defeated and captured him in 203 BCE, and he died in Roman captivity.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/syphax.jpg" alt="Syphax" width="320" height="163" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Syphax.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the late third century BCE the lands west of Carthage were held by two Berber peoples, the Massylii in the east and the larger Masaesyli in the west, whose king <b>Syphax</b> ruled from Siga and later from Cirta.</blockquote><a href="/empire/numidia">Numidia · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>By the late 3rd century BCE they formed a kingdom ruled from Siga, near the mouth of the Tafna river, with a second capital at Cirta after <b>Syphax</b> conquered eastern lands.</blockquote><a href="/state/masaesyli">Masaesyli</a></li><li><blockquote>After Gaia's death the throne passed through Oezalces, Capussa and Lacumazes amid civil war, while <b>Syphax</b> of the Masaesyli seized Massylian lands.</blockquote><a href="/state/massylii">Massylii</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Aïn Témouchent, in what is now <a href="/countries/algeria">Algeria</a>. Died in Tivoli. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=35.3,-1.14&amp;year=-212" aria-label="Aïn Témouchent on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4521 887 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Syphax"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4971 1157h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4971 1157h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=35.3,-1.14&amp;year=-212">What was here in 212 BCE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
